   "stem": {
      "text": "The function \\( f \\) has derivatives of all orders for all real \\( x \\). It satisfies \\( f(1) = 2 \\) and \\( f'(x) = x f(x) - 3 \\) for all \\( x \\)."
   },
   "skills": [
      "BC-SKL-10043",
      "BC-SKL-10044",
      "BC-SKL-10046"
   ],
   "parts": [
      {
         "id": "a",
         "prompt": "Find \\( f''(x) \\) in terms of \\( x \\), \\( f(x) \\) and \\( f'(x) \\). Then find the value of \\( f''(1) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "f''(1) = 1",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Differentiate x f(x) - 3 with the product rule.",
               "latex": "f''(x) = f(x) + x f'(x)"
            },
            {
               "text": "From the relation, f'(1) = 1 \\cdot 2 - 3 = -1.",
               "latex": "f'(1) = -1"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate at x = 1.",
               "latex": "f''(1) = 2 + 1\\cdot(-1) = 1"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "a1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99022",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-10043"
               ],
               "criterion": "Applies the product rule to x f(x) to get f''(x) = f(x) + x f'(x); the constant -3 contributes nothing.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": null
            },
            {
               "point_id": "a2",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99027",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-10043"
               ],
               "criterion": "Finds f'(1) = -1 and gives f''(1) = 1.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": {
                  "kind": "sympy_equivalence",
                  "target": "answer",
                  "expected": "1",
                  "up_to_constant": false,
                  "variable": "x"
               },
               "follows_from": [
                  "a1"
               ]
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "b",
         "prompt": "Find \\( f'''(x) \\) in terms of \\( x \\), \\( f'(x) \\) and \\( f''(x) \\), and find the value of \\( f'''(1) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "f'''(1) = -1",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Differentiate f''(x) = f(x) + x f'(x); the product x f'(x) gives f'(x) + x f''(x).",
               "latex": "f'''(x) = 2f'(x) + x f''(x)"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate at x = 1.",
               "latex": "f'''(1) = 2(-1) + 1\\cdot 1 = -1"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "b1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99022",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-10043"
               ],
               "criterion": "Applies the product rule to x f'(x) to get f'''(x) = 2f'(x) + x f''(x), or an equivalent expression.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": null
            },
            {
               "point_id": "b2",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99027",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-10043"
               ],
               "criterion": "Gives f'''(1) = -1.",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": {
                  "kind": "sympy_equivalence",
                  "target": "answer",
                  "expected": "-1",
                  "up_to_constant": false,
                  "variable": "x"
               },
               "follows_from": [
                  "a1",
                  "a2",
                  "b1"
               ]
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Write the third-degree Taylor polynomial for \\( f \\) about \\( x = 1 \\), and use it to approximate \\( f(1.2) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "2 - (x - 1) + \\frac{(x - 1)^{2}}{2} - \\frac{(x - 1)^{3}}{6}, \\quad f(1.2) \\approx \\frac{682}{375} \\approx 1.819",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Each coefficient is the derivative value at 1 divided by the matching factorial.",
               "latex": "2 + (-1)(x - 1) + \\frac{1}{2!}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{-1}{3!}(x - 1)^{3}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Simplify.",
               "latex": "P_{3}(x) = 2 - (x - 1) + \\frac{(x - 1)^{2}}{2} - \\frac{(x - 1)^{3}}{6}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Substitute x = 1.2, so x - 1 = 0.2.",
               "latex": "P_{3}(1.2) = 2 - 0.2 + 0.02 - \\frac{0.008}{6} = \\frac{682}{375}"
            },
            {
               "text": "State the approximation.",
               "latex": "f(1.2) \\approx \\frac{682}{375} \\approx 1.819"
            }
         ],
         "points": [
            {
               "point_id": "c1",
               "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99035",
               "skills": [
                  "BC-SKL-10044"
               ],
               "criterion": "Writes the first two terms, 2 - (x - 1), in powers of (x - 1).",
               "eligible_only_if": [],
               "check": null,
               "follows_from": [
                  "a2"
               ]
            },
            {
